members.doc:
The current quote for one symbol, read from one of your terminals on that broker's server.
`state` says whether the market can be traded (`open`, `closed_session`, ...);
`broker_time` is the broker's own clock, which is not UTC.

types.doc:
A stream message (or a webhook's body: `type` and the event's fields) as the copy event it is,
or null for any other type. Narrow on `type` to read its payload:

```ts
const event = copyEventOf(message);
if (event?.type === "copy.refused") console.log(event.data.reason, event.data.venue_code);
```

members.doc:
One page of your leaders' signals, newest first, each with `outcomes`: how many of its own
copies were filled, refused and skipped. `kind` and `action` go comma-separated, checked here;
the window is at most 31 days, the last 24 hours without `from`.
